is your company equipped to deal with  software development and delivery  as it adopts technologies like  containers hybrid cloud or even  multi-cloud  yes no maybe well keep watching as we  unwrap the modern ci cd  with and those  [Music]  i'm priyanka vergaria and welcome to  anthos 101  in this episode we're talking about all  things cicd  on your journey to container adoption  across hybrid and multi-cloud  environments  it is important to think seriously about  continuous integration and continuous  delivery  oftentimes you will see operations teams  getting bigger  security best practices tougher to  enforce over  more environments and reliability issues  making their way  into production so let's unwrap hybrid  and multi-cloud continuous integration  and continuous delivery  an approach that can help you accelerate  your release cycles  and increase your software reliability  across all your environments  modern ci cd on anthos embraces a  shift-left  approach to development and leverages  declarative templates to manage security  policy not people  this means that issues are addressed  during build and test phase  not in production it allows you to bring  your operations teams together  cutting down on silos and the  proliferation of tools  so let's dive in when we think about the  creation of a ci cd pipeline there are  three different teams that are involved  developers operators and security  engineers  in this model developers have their own  git repository where they store their  application code  that application code can kick off  continuous integration  whenever a developer creates a commit a  change to their application code  a continuous integration tool tests the  code and then creates an  artifact when we're talking about  deploying to kubernetes clusters our  artifacts are container images that will  eventually be pushed to production  once continuous integration creates that  container image  it will store it in container registry  the reference to the recently stored  image will be stored in  another git repository controlled by  your application operations team  we'll call this the deployment repo this  secondary repository holds kubernetes  manifests  which have instructions on how  applications should be configured  in order to manage that configuration we  use a tool called customize  customize packages together the desired  state container image from our container  registry  and the instructions from the kubernetes  manifests and  store it in the deployment repository  this git repository stores the state  that we want to deploy  into our environments the first place  where we store that state  is within the staging branch of the  deployment repository  from that staging branch a continuous  delivery tool  manages the deployment to our staging  environment  where developers can test this  application  with and those consistent platform the  staging environments are more similar to  your production environments  think about problems created with  different tools practices and processes  when testing in the cloud  and then pushing to production in a  totally different environment  when the developers have finished  testing they can tell the operators that  they want to make a push to production  or the operators can control the timing  to push to production  they merge from the staging branch of  the deployment repository into the  master branch  and propagate those changes into  production environment  for our security teams let's talk a  minute about how to secure your  production environments  you also have your own git repository  that is going to store the expected  state of the security policies  things like role-based access control  policies  coders for your applications and  restricting risky behaviors such as the  ability for containers to run as root  how can you do that well one mechanism  we use  is the policy controller which is a part  of config management  because of and those consistent platform  across all of your environments security  teams can customize what policies they  want to run  in what groups of clusters and this is  all done without having to configure it  in each environment that was a quick  overview of modern ci cd on andos  showing how you can increase your  development velocity and produce  safe reliable applications for your  customers  ready to get started check out the  solutions page linked below  and for more anthers content don't  forget to subscribe and  follow the anthos 101 playlist
 

